{
  "description": "Hand-maintained mapping from every icon key (the catalog's product and type icon keys, plus the generic marks) to its artwork. Each key names candidate sources in fallback order: 'own' (a gcportrait drawing under own/), 'core' (Google's core product colour mark, for marquee products), 'legacy' (Google's two-tone console icon), then 'category' (the Google category mark of the product's category, a key of 'categories', as Google's product icons overview assigns it), which is also the key's category. scripts/vendor.mjs takes the first candidate that exists in the downloaded sets and fails when none does; scripts/build.mjs compiles the result into src/generated/icons.ts. Source paths are entry names inside the zip files listed under 'sources'. 'legibility16' is the 16 px legibility check list: for each candidate glyph, whether the official icon stays or an own drawing replaces it (scripts/contact-sheet.mjs renders it). See README.md.",
